      ":question/worked-solution": "Since our circle is centered at the origin and has a radius of $\\sqrt{5},$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}={\\sqrt{5}}^{2}\\,\u27f9\\,{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=5.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(5) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"
